# SHOW AS SITE LAW — PREVIEWS = LIVE LAYOUT

**Status: MANDATORY · NON-NEGOTIABLE.** Owner locked 2026-07-12.  
**Change this law only with owner passcode `4444`.**  
**Canonical prose:** [`SHOW_AS_SITE_LAW.md`](../../SHOW_AS_SITE_LAW.md)

## The rule

Whenever you show the owner something for **approval, audit, review, or spot-check**, render it **the way it will appear on the live site** — not a fake admin card, not a truncated label, not a mystery crop.

## Face / mosaic image boards (GTM, KPI, Rev Arch, …)

Site tiles (`index.html` `ftile` + `css/pulse-mosaic.css`):

1. **Photo** fills the tile (`object-fit: cover`) — clean face, **no baked title**
2. **Pillar chip** (`mm-cat`) — e.g. REVENUE ARCHITECTURE
3. **Full question title** as yellow `h4` over the scrim — **industry lives in that title** (readable)

Approval rooms **must** match that shape:

- **Square** face photo (`aspect-ratio: 1/1`, cover)
- Pillar chip on the photo
- **Full question title under the square** (no line-clamp) so industry is always readable

Vote buttons sit under the title.

## Do

- Use the real `question` / title string the index will publish
- Keep industry visible in the title text (that is how the site shows it)
- Prefer linking `/css/pulse-mosaic.css` or copying its tile CSS so previews do not drift

## Do not

- Hide the industry in tiny footer text only
- Invent a different card chrome that does not match mosaic tiles
- Bake titles into the JPG for review (visual lock still owns images)

## Bypass

Only with owner passcode **`4444`**.
